  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform cubical box of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed&nbsp;on a rough floor and it is to be moved by applying minimum possible force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> at a point which is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;above its centre of mass. If the coefficient of friction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then what is the maximum possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math> for which the box will not topple before moving?\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "50.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For no toppling&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>μ</mi><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>(in limiting case )</p><p>But it is not possible as maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> can be equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi></math> only</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn></math></p>"
  }
}